course: dictionary
lesson: 5270
title: Joyous and the power of a stronger word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you meet a word you know a little, like happy, read the words around it. They are its context, and they show you how strong it is. «They row Portly back, set him down on the tow-path near the ford, and watch him waddle off until Otter leaps up from the shallows with an amazed and joyous bark.» Otter is amazed, so the bark is full of surprise and delight.
explain: Ask: what would fit here? Happy would fit, but try it: «an amazed and happy bark» still makes sense, so joyous is close to happy. Joyous is a stronger, warmer word. It means full of joy, and it is very happy, not just a little pleased.
explain: Joyous can also describe something that causes great joy. A joyous occasion is a day that makes everyone glad, like a family coming home after a long time away.
fact: Joyous is an adjective: joyous, more joyous, most joyous.
fact: «Joyous» means full of joy; very happy.
fact: «Joyous» can also mean causing great joy, as in «a joyous occasion».
fact: Writers use joyous in stories, hymns and carols, and it is stronger than happy.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows there are joyous feasts and the joyous return of Toad Hall.
exercise: «Otter leaps up from the shallows with an amazed and joyous bark.» What does joyous mean here? | Quiet and sleepy | Angry and loud | *Full of joy and very happy | Dirty and wet
exercise: Which would most likely be a joyous occasion? | *A family homecoming with hugs and cheers | A long, dull wait for a bus | A broken toy | A cold, empty room
exercise: In writing, why might an author choose joyous instead of happy? | It means the same as sad | *It is a stronger, warmer word that shows great joy | It is only used for animals | It is shorter, so it is easier to read
test: «The villagers held a joyous feast when the king came home.» Which word tells you the feast was very happy? | held | Villagers | *joyous | king
test: Christmas and Easter are called joyous festivals in church. What is the best meaning of joyous? | Lost and afraid | Dull and grey | Very sad and quiet | *Full of joy; very happy
exam: Sam says joyous is just another word for happy. Which answer is best? | Joyous is only the name of a town | Joyous means the same as angry | *Joyous is a stronger, warmer word, full of great joy | Joyous means sleepy
